 "notes": {
  "method": "MERL zero-shot (Liu et al., ICML 2024, arXiv 2403.06659), official code and released checkpoint, no training or fine-tuning on any of our data.",
  "pretraining_data": "MIMIC-IV-ECG v1.0 (BIDMC, Boston; 771,693 ECG-report pairs, 500 Hz, 10 s). It shares no records with our databases (CPSC2018/CPSC-Extra, PTB-XL, Georgia, Shaoxing/Ningbo), which come from other hospitals and countries.",
  "checkpoint_selection_caveat": "The released *_best_ckpt.pth was selected during pretraining by the average zero-shot AUROC on the validation splits of PTB-XL (super/sub/form/rhythm), CPSC2018 (ICBEB) and Chapman-Shaoxing (CSN) (see utils/utils_trainer.py and pretrain/config.yaml val_sets). Those are part of our CPSC, PTBXL and SHAONING test sets. MERL never trained on them, but it was model-selected on them, and its CKEPE prompts were written for their class names. GEORGIA was never used.",
  "paper_eval": "The paper evaluates zero-shot on PTB-XL (4 subsets), CPSC2018 and CSN test splits, with dataset-specific label sets. Our evaluation uses our SNOMED vocabulary and protocol, so the numbers are not comparable to the paper's."
 },
